            <ArticleTitle>Calcified embolus of the left coronary ostia after aortic valve replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1162-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a left coronary calcified embolus causing acute myocardial dysfunction immediately after aortic valve replacement is described. Prompt diagnosis by transesophageal echocardiogram was made, which led to removal of the embolus and a subsequent satisfactory course.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
